A||||3||VAROOM||Won't Start ???||||5||
Z||000000||VAROOM||03-06-2000||10:20 AM||||Well all you master minds. This one is for you. Changed the IM, The coil, and it runs great till you do long distance, shut it off let it sit for twenty minutes, and it wont start. Tryed the thing with the peddel, the injectors arn't leaking. seems the thing just shuts down untill it cools off, then it starts just great. when its hot it turns over fine. Any Ideas Thanx. VAROOM||||reg||5
Z||000001||wwh0001||03-06-2000||12:58 PM||||When you say it won't start, does it have a spark ?  Will it fire or just turn over. If it is not fuel related then ignition would be the next item. When you turn it over check for spark ( spark plug wire off palce next to metal and see if ther is a spark) You replaced your ignition module and Coil? was that the ingition coil ? If so did you replace your Pick up Coil? Heat destroys them. Heat can do stange things to electrical items. If they overheat they can fail.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||03-06-2000||08:11 PM||||have you checked your fuel pump? if the fuel pump is getting hot it will shut itself off and whe it cools it works perectly, this happened t me in my t,a and i found out that my pump was shorting out, and once it cooled down it would work, have it checked, good luck, al.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bob Englert||03-06-2000||09:06 PM||||Did you add the dielectric (sp?) grease under the ignition module when you installed it? On my 88 Formula, the instructions said to coat the back side of the module to insulate the module from heat from the distibutor.  The manual was pretty specific about this as I remember. THis might explain the need to let if cool down before running again.||||reg||1
